{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for M1 developer Source6aa1e6f0e040ca4257a4d3801467018e5a1fc375, tree d4953ee674a374e3d6c4bf5afd7f98997b33386c, against approved G0 Main9c32a3843feb68af4119c34c2afbf10c06222ee9. One finding from the complete33-path review.\n\nF1 — P2: serve the preview at the package entry's canonical URL. packages/cli/src/application-dev.ts:126–130 aliases \"/\" to presentation.entry but sends its HTML without changing the browser's base URL. The compiler correctly emits script/CSS beside that entry. For a valid entry screens/index.html, the default preview therefore resolves ./application.js as /application.js (404), while the actual asset is /screens/application.js (200). The inspection panel's iframe at line36 also uses \"/\", so the package is broken in the ordinary dev flow even though pack/check accepts it. Existing application-pack.test.ts explicitly witnesses a nested entry, but the dev tests only use root index.html.\n\nIndependent actual localhost probe7a84cc reproduces this using the unchanged generated starter with only presentation.entry changed to screens/index.html: root HTML200; /application.js404; /screens/application.js200. Fix the default preview and panel to use the entry's canonical path, or redirect \"/\" there while preserving package-relative asset semantics. Keep reload/service routes correct without changing signed package bytes. Add an owning dev regression that follows the default preview/panel navigation and resolves its script and CSS, including a nested entry. This is a functional URL-resolution failure, not a claim about installed-host routes.\n\nScope/provenance. Primarya0633a16 was read first and in full (204 lines), then all new source/tests/data/docs and the complete existing-file diffs, with the previously approved foundation as unchanged basis. Verified all2,156 candidate leaves:2,123 prior Main rows unchanged, exactly33 changed paths (14 additions/19 modifications), including preserved G0. Both artifa